       --ff ffiilleennaammee
              This  option  indicates  the zone file mode. Instead of a public
              keyfile name, the argument is the DNS domain name of a zone mas‐
              ter file, which can be read from ffiilleennaammee. If the domain name is
              the same as ffiilleennaammee, then it may be omitted.

              If ffiilleennaammee is set to ""--"", then the zone data is read  from  the
              standard input.

       --KK ddiirreeccttoorryy
              This option sets the directory in which the key files are to re‐
              side.

       --LL ttttll This  option sets the default TTL to use for this key when it is
              converted into a DNSKEY RR. This is the TTL used when the key is
              imported into a zone, unless there was already a DNSKEY RRset in
              place, in which case the existing TTL takes precedence.  Setting
              the default TTL to 00 or nnoonnee removes it from the key.

       --hh     This option emits a usage message and exits.

       --vv lleevveell
